From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sim: do not walk a freed watch list in open_channel_cb

open_channel_cb() notifies each session watcher while iterating the
watch list, and only advances the iterator after notify() returns. A
watcher may remove its own watch from inside notify(), which frees both
the watchlist item and the GSList node the loop is standing on. The
following g_slist_next() then reads freed memory.

simfs does exactly that when the driver fails a session read
synchronously: get_session_cb() -> session_read_info() -> failure ->
sim_fs_op_error() -> sim_fs_end_current() ->
__ofono_sim_remove_session_watch(). ofono-binder-plugin implements
session_read_info as a stub that calls back immediately with an error,
so any SIM with an ISIM application (VoLTE SIMs, read for EFimpi in
discover_apps_cb) takes ofonod down. Observed on the Unihertz Titan
Pocket: "SIM card OK", "session_read_info not implemented", SIGSEGV,
30 restarts in a row and no telephony.

Advance the iterator before calling notify().

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/sim.c
+++ b/src/sim.c
@@ -4034,9 +4034,14 @@
 		struct ofono_watchlist_item *item = iter->data;
 		ofono_sim_session_event_cb_t notify = item->notify;
 
-		notify(active, session->session_id, item->notify_data);
-
+		/*
+		 * Step past this node before calling out: the watcher may
+		 * remove its own watch from inside notify(), which frees
+		 * both item and the list node iter points at.
+		 */
 		iter = g_slist_next(iter);
+
+		notify(active, session->session_id, item->notify_data);
 	}
 }
 
